                <pb facs="0921" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg777"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9331/129: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-22T20:00:00+08:00">January 22, 1929—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 22—8:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>46. Reference Legation’s 45, January 22, 7 p.m. As to paragraph 5, Department’s
                    9, January 7, 6 p.m. In view of previous experience concerning the unreliability
                    of similar oral assurances, the receipt of a satisfactory written reply to the
                    American request for an assurance regarding the construction to be given to
                    provisions for nondiscriminatory treatment will, I assume, be awaited before
                    further action is taken on the treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
